    'sg.alarm.sub': 'Smoke, gas, water, alarm panel, window in the rain, message to your phone',
    'sg.alarm.help': 'Warnings appear at the top as a red banner, the room flashes red, a tap jumps into the room. Nothing to set up: the add-on finds smoke, gas, carbon monoxide and water sensors and the alarm panel of Home Assistant by itself. Whether a window warns in the rain is set in the window\'s properties.',
    'sg.alarm.what': 'What does “alarm panel” mean?',
    'sg.alarm.whatHelp': 'An alarm panel in Home Assistant (for example from the free integration “Alarmo” via HACS, or from a real alarm system). Which doors, windows and motion sensors set it off is chosen there, not here. The add-on shows when it goes off and can send a message. Put the alarm panel into the plan as a device to arm and disarm it there. Without Alarmo it works too: with the holiday alarm just below.',
